implementationPlan.description:
Mutation proof (DoD 1). Run it in a scratch snapshot, never in the worktree.

From the worktree root, under the lease, run /mnt/d/moe-scratch/fb0ab382-plan/mutant.sh byte for byte; its sha256 is in SHA256SUMS there. The script:
1. archives HEAD's moe-jetbrains into /mnt/d/moe-scratch/fb0ab382-mutant. A test-only snapshot needs no packages dist (mem:gotcha-jetbrains-snapshot-gradle-test);
2. copies in your test file;
3. rewrites `(runs + roots + tree + watched)` to `(runs + tree + watched)` in the snapshot's MoeDaemonSupervisor.kt, and asserts there is exactly one hit;
4. runs the class.

The Gradle run must exit non-zero, and W36 must be the only failed row. On 2026-10-30 QA's run of the probes against the same mutant showed 77 tests and 1 failure, QA1.

Keep the console tail for the completion summary. Remove the snapshot afterwards; it is only your own scratch directory.

Verification, once, before moe.complete_task (DoD 2).

Under the jetbrains-gradle lease, run the checkRef from the worktree root, byte for byte as /mnt/d/moe-scratch/fb0ab382-plan/verify.sh. It runs, in order:
- parity-check;
- lint;
- the DoD's `gradlew.bat test --rerun` through cmd.exe in this worktree's moe-jetbrains. This is the Windows form of the DoD command, because WSL has no JDK;
- the JUnit XML totals, which fail on any failure or error.
Its fresh output is the complete_task evidence.

Also show that `git diff --stat $(git merge-base HEAD moe/work-2026-10-24) -- moe-jetbrains/src/main` prints nothing: no production byte changed.

Release the lease on every path. Never run clean. Never pattern-kill a Gradle or Java process.
